@@ -167,11 +167,12 @@ Related: [Toolbar](Toolbar) · [Inspector](Inspector) · [GPS Track Recording](G
 
 ## The map clock gets out of the way
 
-The time strip lies across the bottom of the chart, and the deck's own strip along the top
-already carries its readout beside the Zulu clock. So on a phone it **goes away when nothing
-answers to it** — no NOTAM, no weather, no wind, no open airfield panel — and comes straight
-back when something does. A live position hides it either way: the hour being flown is now.
-
-On a desktop it dims instead. There is room for it, it has a fixed place, and a control that
-vanishes from a fixed place is one a pilot hunts for. `hideIdleMapClockOnPhone` puts it back
-on a phone too.
+On a phone the clock lives in the top strip. The hour the layers are showing sits there beside
+the Zulu time (*11:00Z ▾*, or *+3h · 14:00Z* when you have moved it), and it is a button: tap it
+and the slider opens as **one row under the strip** — **Now**, the hour, and the slider. Tap the
+hour again, or press **Now** (back to live), and the row folds away. Closed, it takes no map at
+all. A live position hides it: the hour being flown is now.
+
+On a desktop the clock lies across the bottom of the chart and dims when nothing answers to it.
+There is room for it, it has a fixed place, and a control that vanishes from a fixed place is one
+a pilot hunts for.
